; VU1 microprogram (generated by tools/vu1/gen.py fx, do not edit): effect particles (fx.c). One input vertex of
; 3 qw per particle; the program moves it (drag and gravity, closed form), looks up its size / colour curves, rolls,
; projects and expands it into a 4-vertex triangle strip (the first two vertices of each particle carry ADC, so the
; strip restarts per particle). Two loops: camera-facing quads (fxGrp) and quads fixed in the effect frame (fxoGrp,
; header 0.y != 0: FFX Orientation 2, the fog-wall sheets).
; Constants: 0-3 view matrix columns, 4 scale (F, -F, Zs, fog a), 5 offset (cx, cy, 0, fog b) (vu1_begin +
; vu1_map_fog), 8-12 sin / cos coefficients (.xy) and motion series (.zw: phi2, phi1), 13 motion constants
; (2^-5, 0, 2^(5-1), 0), (0, 0, 1/2, 1) (vu1_fx_begin). Batch (input buffer, BASE 16 / OFFSET 313):
; 0 {particles (even), oriented, -, -}, 1 (cw, ch, 0.5, 1 / fpr), 2 (0.5 / W - cw / 2, 0.5 / H, 0, fpr), 3 (du, dv, 0,
; edge fog a2), 4 (du, 0, 0, 0), 5 (0, dv, 0, 0), 6 (fog min, fog max, 0, 2048), 7 A+D GIF tag (6 regs: TEX0 TEX1 TEST
; ALPHA ZBUF FOGCOL, EOP) + 8-13, 14 PRIM tag template (EOP, triangle strip, STQ RGBAQ XYZF2), 15 / 16 the quad's world
; x / y axes (oriented batches), 17.. 8 curve tables of 8 keys x {size (kx, ky, drag, gravity), colour (r, g, b, a)
; as integers} (drag / gravity: the VIF row, masked unpack), 145.. particles: {spawn xyz, 8 table + 7 age / life},
; {half size x, y, roll (-pi..pi), frame + 0.5}, {spawn velocity xyz, age}. cw / ch: flipbook cell, du / dv = cell - 1
; texel (normalized).
; Motion (fx.c ppos): p = p0 + v0 t phi1(d t) + (0, gravity, 0) t^2 phi2(d t), phi1(x) = (1 - e^-x) / x, phi2(x) =
; (x - 1 + e^-x) / x^2: series at y = x 2^-5 (y <= 1/2), then 5 doublings of (E, phi2, phi1): E' = E^2,
; the .zw series hold 2^5 phi2 and phi1, so the doubling keeps G (phi1) and H (2^5 phi2) unscaled:
; G' = G (1 + E), H' = H (1 + E) / 2 + 2^(5-1) G, then g = t' G, h = t'^2 H with t' = t 2^-5.
; Per particle: view v = M p; key k, f from .w: size = mix(K_k, K_k+1, f) x half size, colour likewise; corner =
; centre + qx A + qy B with A = (hx cos, hy sin), B = (-hx sin, hy cos) (roll, then size, as fx.c's EE path);
; screen xy at q = 1 / v.z; depth and fog at z' = v.z - max(hx, hy) (pulled toward the camera, fx.c); fog =
; min(clamp(a z' + b, fmin, fmax), max(b + a2 z', 0)); cell (col, row) of frame n: row = trunc(n / fpr).
; Oriented: corner = v + qx G + qy H with G = c U + s W, H = c W - s U, U = hx M X, W = hy M Y; each corner its own
; q, depth and fog (no pull).
; sin / cos: half angle polynomials (x <= pi / 2), then the double angle (|error| < 2e-4).
; Output slots 642 / 811 (1 + 12 x 14 qw, alternating; VI08 keeps the next across batches).

; loops: 60 cycles per particle to move, 88 to draw (oriented 120) in the tools/vu1 timing model (2 per pass)
; layout: FX_IN 16 (313 qw each), FX_OUT0 642, FX_OUT1 811 (169 qw each), end 980

		.vu
		.align 4
		.global VU1Fx_CodeStart
		.global VU1Fx_CodeEnd
